WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.480
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.480
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.770
Christmas Eve

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.770
Narrow Window

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.770
Early Wins

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.770
Take Friends

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.770
Omisoka

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.280
All right.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.010
Preparations for tomorrow are all done.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:16.120
Aren't we still taking hanabira 
mochi orders for Shogatsu?

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.670
Only for our long-time regular customers.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.960
We have to go give our greetings 
and do our graveside visits.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.840
Is this leftovers?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.600
Yes, you can do as you like with it.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.790
If you don't use it, put it away.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:32.170
Oh, you! Why can't you just say, 
"you can go ahead and practice"?

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:32.840
Moron!

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.450
You can practice,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.260
but, originally, hanabira mochi

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.320
was created from the hishihanabira 
mochi served in the imperial court

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.830
for the first Urasenke 
tea ceremony of the year.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.930
Gobo root, which is simmered for three 
days and three nights to make it sweet,

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:52.250
is wrapped in white miso an, which is dyed a 
pale crimson, and sweet gyuuhi mochi.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.570
For the sake of our patrons who like 
ours and have chosen it above others,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.630
we can't make any bad ones.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:03.630
Make sure you pound that into your head.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.920
Yeah. I know.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.360
Oh! The new year is here!

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.010
Is it?

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.310
Congratulations on the start of the new year.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.160
Yes. Congratulations.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.930
I'll be counting on you this year, too.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:34.860
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:02.410
<b>Reminiscing About Waiting for Spring</b>

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:11.480
Oh, hey!

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.590
What's this? And I thought 
I'd be the first one here.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:17.700
Oh!

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.760
It's the First Sunrise!

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.590
Wow.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.140
Congrats on the start of the new year.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.940
Yes, congratulations.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.400
The kind made with clear 
sumashi soup is good,

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.900
but, yeah, ozoni soup really has to be 
white miso soup with round mochi in it!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.160
We have a lot more if you want seconds.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.690
I do! I do!

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:45.020
Itsuka.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:45.490
Yes?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.380
Here. Your otoshidama.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.660
Thank you.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.880
I hope you'll be a good girl this year, too.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.590
I will.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.560
It's great to get Otoshidama!

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.140
Oh. Could you consider that to 
be from the whole Irino family?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.720
I'm kidding. Stop staring in silence.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.600
I have an envelope.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.180
<b>Otoshidama</b>

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.180
Here. This is from me.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.600
Thank you.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.050
Oh, right.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.250
I have one delivery for you to do later.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.900
Huh? We have a delivery?

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:18.300
Coming!

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.030
Congratulations on the start of the new year!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.750
We've come to pick up our hanabira mochi!

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.320
We've come!

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.820
Congratulations to you, too. 
Just a moment, please.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.410
Oh, would you like some ozoni before you go?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:36.320
We're going to a relative's house now!

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.460
Going!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.520
We're visiting my husband's parents
 and making a family trip out of it.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.080
That's wonderful.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.100
In that case, you'll be able 
to eat lots of delicious food.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.050
Yeah!

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.790
Well, be careful!

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.810
We will!

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:49.550
Let's go.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.530
I want to hurry up and get there!

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.540
I'll be back in a bit.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.480
All right. Be careful.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.400
<b>Notice Regarding Business Hours

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:04.860
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.260
We're only filling pre-orders today.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.870
Oh, really? I'm sorry for troubling you.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.210
Ugh, it's freezing!

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.010
Oh.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.660
It's him.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.680
Excuse me.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:34.480
We met earlier, in front of the shop.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:41.820
My mother's grave is nearby, you see.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:46.320
I've left the tending of her grave 
to relatives for a long time, but...

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.910
Lately, bad things keep 
happening one after another.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.910
What do you mean?

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.630
Fracturing my pinkie toe, stepping on
 my glasses and breaking them...

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:01.760
Arguing with my wife and getting kicked,
 hard, right in the face.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:02.750
Wow...

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.160
I wanted to show my regret for 
my previous neglect,

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:12.510
and I thought that I could at least offer 
her favorite Ryokushou sweets, but...

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.020
Even in this, I'm unlucky. I just 
can't help feeling that way.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:23.050
I know that I have to go, 
but my feet just won't go.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.130
Um, I might have a suggestion.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.120
Won't you become an acquaintance of mine?

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.300
Huh?

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.020
Nagomu-san is taking a long time, isn't he?

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.440
Honestly, should we leave 
him and go on our hatsumode?

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:49.380
<i>He's probably just dawdling 
along on his way back.</i>

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.760
It couldn't be...

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.590
Nagomu-san?

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:03.900
What have you been doing all—

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.730
Shh!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.400
You're giving out the hanabira 
mochi you made for practice?!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.860
You know you can't do that! 
You're going to get yelled at!

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.580
I know! I know, but...

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:19.640
He came all the way here because 
he wanted to offer her our sweets.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.620
It makes me happy, you know?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:32.590
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:28.560
I know that what I've made 
for training can't be sold...

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.590
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.220
But I thought it wouldn't matter 
if I gave them to an acquaintance.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.440
I made them for practice,

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.970
but the an, the sweet gyuuhi mochi, and the 
gobo root all have the Ryokushou flavor.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.980
I'm sure Buddha will forgive me for this much.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.740
I'll go get a bag.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:52.860
I'm in training, too, so it should 
be fine for me to help you, right?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.920
We're in the same boat.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.700
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.880
A-Are you sure?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.800
Thank you so much!

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.290
How much should I pay you?

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.540
Oh, there's no need.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:11.000
I made those sweets in training, 
so they aren't well-made.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.840
If I took money for those, I'd get clobbered.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:17.160
Besides, I'm giving them to you 
because you're an acquaintance.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.860
If you were a customer, I could
 never let you have them.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.700
Even though you say these aren't well-made,

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:28.820
they are more than good enough 
for me to offer at a graveside.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.520
I'm sure she's waiting for you to come visit.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:34.240
Please go see her.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:37.310
Next time, I'll come as a customer.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.860
We'll be waiting.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.250
<b>Kadonaga Family</b>

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.670
<b>Kadonaga Family Grave</b>

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.300
It's delicious.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.520
The neighborhood sure is quiet.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.000
Everyone's gone to the big places.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.190
It's nice that we can take 
our time with our visit.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.250
Congratulations to you!

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.910
Congratulations to you!

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.040
Did you come here last year, too?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:22.950
Yes.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.810
What did you ask for?

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.770
You have no tact.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.630
You're right. I'm sorry.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:35.110
<i>Last year, I wished that 
I could find Papa soon.</i>

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.260
Here we go... Huh?

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.490
Here we go!

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:48.760
Now, shall we pay our respects?

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:54.730
If you wish with all your heart, 
your wishes are sure to come true, right?

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:59.320
You think so? I've heard that the 
deities here tend to cut corners.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:00.570
Really?

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.800
Well, the gods must be busy.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:07.790
If they grant even a little of a wish, 
maybe we can forgive them for the rest.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:11.130
I already forgave them a long time ago.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:20.120
<i>I wish for everyone at Ryokushou to 
be healthy and happy in the next year.</i>

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.220
<i>And...</i>

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:26.090
<i>I wish for Nagomu-san to be just a 
little more serious about things.</i>

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:36.100
I wish that a certain someone would stop 
saying that his sweets aren't well-made.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.110
<i>Are we busted?</i>

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:43.530
"When the wind blows from the east, let it
 carry your scent to me, plum blossoms.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.570
And though your guest may not 
be here, do not forget the spring."

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:51.150
The buds of the plum are 
starting to swell, aren't they?

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.990
It may be cold now, but it's 
almost spring, isn't it...

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:55.930
Koume?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.630
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.760
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.970
<b>Furled Crimson</b>

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.970
Oh, what lovely sweets!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.390
<b>This Month's Sweets
 Furled Crimson
 With matcha
 A la carte (can be ordered to go)</b>

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.390
What is the motif for this?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:08.220
Furled Crimson depicts the plum blossom buds
 that bloom around the first day of spring.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:12.730
Really? Then this sweet is something 
we can get around Setsubun.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.230
Yes, it is.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:17.950
Then I'll have the Furled Crimson
 with matcha, please.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.100
So will I.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.530
That's two sets, correct?

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.220
Speaking of which...

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.520
You're going to the Setsubun festival, right?

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:27.180
With Kanoko and Mitsuru-chan. 
The three of you together.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.100
Yes.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.910
I hope things will be... peaceful.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:31.870
<i>Peaceful?</i>

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.910
Hello!

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:36.710
Oh, Otsurusan!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.630
But you're not working today.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.750
Harumi said she wouldn't be able 
to make it home at the usual time,

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.980
so I went to pick them up from 
preschool instead, but...

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.180
I was the one who said it!

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.640
I said that I wanted to 
eat sweets from Ryokushou.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:54.020
Did you? Well, thank you 
for coming, Yuu-chan, Koume-chan.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.500
Stop it, Obachan.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.360
Call me Monaka!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.640
M-Monaka?

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:01.720
Koume!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:06.110
In the anime <i>Fashion Transformation 
Sweets Squadron, Pate☆Puri</i>,

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.950
that's the name of the 
peach-blossom-colored girl.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:11.390
There are five of them and they each have 
a sweet that they're good at, right?

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:12.370
That's right!

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.830
Monaka-chan is good at wagashi.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.520
And my last name is Momonose, like "peach 
rapids," and she's peach-blossom-colored.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.400
Oh! Nagomu-chan!

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:20.960
Uh-oh!

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.590
Special Skill...

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.760
Mitarashi Heaven Bomber!

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.330
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.330
Koume!

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.200
I've told you, I hate that name!

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.890
Yes, yes.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.740
What sweet would you like?

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.700
This red one is cute.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.980
Isn't it? It's an ume plum sweet.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.610
Then I won't have it.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.160
I'll have something else.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.070
Yuu-chan wants ozenzai!

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.700
All right. Ozenzai soup for you.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:50.490
I'm sorry! Are my mother and children here?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.950
Oh. Harumi-chan?

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:52.780
Koume!

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:53.960
Harumi...

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:56.270
What did you do to Shige-kun?

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:59.290
What's wrong? Why are you being so loud?

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.970
The preschool got in touch with me.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.990
They said that Koume got into 
a fight with her friend.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.550
Your teacher is really worried about you.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.700
But I mean...

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:13.850
The picture book...

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.230
<i>Umeboshi Granny</i>...

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.220
Umeboshi?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.650
<b>Umeboshi Granny</b>

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:20.650
I hate umeboshi.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:21.320
Why?

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.250
They're sour! And they're all wrinkly.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.450
Oh! Koume, your name has "ume" in it!

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.180
Hey, umeboshi!

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:30.870
You're a wrinkly old granny!

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.980
Mitarashi Heaven Bomber!

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:34.540
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.460
Ume plums aren't cute at all.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.600
They're wrinkly and sour...

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.090
I hate them!

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:45.910
I hate ume plums!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.640
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.640
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:54.810
I'm so very sorry.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.200
And we've stayed so late into the night, too.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.770
She's so tired from crying, 
she's fallen asleep.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.110
Yuu-chan, you must be sleepy, too.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:06.110
I'm glad I learned the reason for 
everything, but... her name, huh?

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.030
It must be difficult for you.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:12.450
It's all right, Mom. She'll understand one day.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:16.620
Nagomu, I'm sorry. Koume's always
 so impudent toward you.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.960
Well... please ask her to use 
her special skill a little less.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.220
That's not going to be possible.

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.950
You and Harumi-san grew 
up together, didn't you?

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.220
Yeah. She's two years older...

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.640
But we were in preschool together.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.740
Still, it's something she'll carry 
with her throughout her life.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.140
I hope she finds a way 
to come to terms with it.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.650
So do I.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:52.240
"When the wind blows from the east, 
let it carry your scent to me, plum blossoms.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.790
And though your guest may not be here,
 do not forget the spring."

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.080
Let's see...

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.080
<b>Confectioners Ryokushou</b>

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.830
Ryokushou is...

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.720
More tea please!

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.040
Here you go.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.020
Itsuka-chan, thank you!

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.010
Koume-chan.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:14.940
Monaka!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.800
Monaka-chan, where are 
your grandma and Yuu-chan?

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.390
Playing at the park.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.020
I didn't want to play, so I came to the shop.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.680
Call Otsurusan!

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.280
I heard from your mom.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:33.800
She said your teacher talked to everyone, 
so they won't tease you anymore.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.200
That's wonderful!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.870
But I hate ume plums. They're not cute.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:40.890
So she still doesn't like them...

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.290
Welcome!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:47.340
Would you like something to go? Or would 
you like to have a seat in our tea shop?

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:51.370
Um, is there someone named Koume here?

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.460
Koume-chan?

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.640
Koume-san? Is that their first name?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.270
Oh, um... It's sort of an old stage name.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.270
A stage name?

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.520
We do have a little Koume-chan 
over there, but...

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.220
Not Koume! Monaka!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.600
Did you come here because you 
heard the name from someone?

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.860
Oh, yes! I'm here on an 
errand from my grandpa.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.130
This is my grandpa a long 
time ago with Koume-san.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.540
I heard that it was about forty years ago.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.710
Oh my. A geiko.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.890
Wait just a moment, please.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:28.180
My husband may know more 
about this than I do.

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:31.600
Let me see.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:32.380
Sure.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.430
This person is Koume-san?

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:38.100
Your name is Koume-chan, right?

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:41.260
My name has "ume" in it too.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.740
I'm Umeka.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:45.260
I hate ume plums.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.270
Huh? Why?

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:50.820
When they turn into umeboshi, 
they're all wrinkly. They're not cute.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:54.220
Oh, I'm sorry! She's gone through 
something a little awful, so...

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:00.120
Koume-chan, have you ever seen plum blossoms?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.040
No.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:05.920
Look. They're so refined, and they're 
little and cute, too, right?

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.210
Umeboshi are sour...

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:12.970
But they're preserved, so you can 
eat them a hundred years from now!

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.130
Isn't that amazing?!

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:17.090
And the meaning of the flowers is lovely, too.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:21.180
The red ones mean "elegance," 
the white ones mean "stately beauty,"

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.820
and the dark pink ones mean "innocence."

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:27.150
Really? Those are all beautiful images.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.870
Nagomu-chan, what does "innocence" mean?

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:31.340
Huh? J-Just a sec.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.860
Oh, here it is. "Unsullied beauty."

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.860
Dictionary

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.860
<b>Innocence</b>

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:35.860
"Unsullied"?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:39.280
Oh, it means that something's 
really clean and pretty.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.260
I see...

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:46.540
Should we ask people in the neighborhood 
about the Koume-san in the photo?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.180
What?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.360
We could even give the neighborhood 
association chair a call and—

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.880
Thank you, but...

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.950
My grandpa might be misremembering, so...

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.460
My grandpa is hospitalized right now.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.760
But when I brought him some 
wagashi that he likes,

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.260
his vacant expression suddenly brightened.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.520
Umeka, I have a favor to ask.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:10.630
There's a wagashi shop called Ryokushou.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.180
There's someone there named Koume...

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.570
...and he said he wanted me 
to give this back to her.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.880
What a pretty kiri wood box.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.800
I don't know what's inside though.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:21.910
Koume...

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.200
Koume will look for Koume-san, too!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.500
Where will you look?

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.360
Places like the temple or the park!

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:28.510
R-Right...

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:29.250
Oh!

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:33.400
If we ask my grandma, she might know!
 Oneechan, let's go together!

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:34.340
What?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.630
I'm sorry. Is Koume-chan...

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:38.720
Grandma!

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:44.010
Grandma, do you know Koume-san? 
They said she's a geiko!

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:44.970
What?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:48.640
The lady over there is looking 
for her. Do you know her?

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.610
K-Koume-san is...

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:57.320
She's come all the way here. 
Wouldn't it be all right to tell her?

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.520
Masa-san.

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:01.660
And there's no need to hide it.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:04.090
Right, Koume-san?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.960
What?

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.390
Well, I'll be going now!

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:42.700
I want to hurry up and tell my grandpa 
that I was able to give it back!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.550
Um, this is from me.

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.220
What?

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.080
Thank you!

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.280
May I open it?

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.380
Oh! These are...

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.560
Furled Crimson!

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.110
They're my grandpa's 
absolute favorite wagashi!

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.510
I'm so glad.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:05.540
Say, Koume...

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:10.150
Once we're together, shall we plant 
a big plum tree in the garden?

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:14.170
I will allow you to date. However...

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.700
If we are speaking of her joining 
our family, that's a different story.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:17.390
Mother!

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:20.030
Think of your standing as 
the heir to the family.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.590
Koume!

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:28.200
Please forgive me!

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:31.330
Even I have my pride!

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.500
Koume!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:47.260
"When the wind blows from the east, 
let it carry your scent to me, plum blossoms.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:47.970
<b>Koume

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:51.890
And though your guest may not 
be here, do not forget the spring."

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.990
<i>O, plum blossoms.</i>

00:20:54.990 --> 00:21:00.250
<i>When the spring winds blow, 
please send me the scent of you.</i>

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:04.970
<i>And though I may not be by 
your side, do not forget the spring.</i>

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:07.510
<i>Right, Koume?</i>

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:15.670
I got the kanji for "plum" in 
Koume and Yuu's names from mom.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:20.300
The path mom carved for herself in 
the arts is one I've always admired.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:24.920
So I put that admiration 
into my children's names.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:26.970
That's really great!

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:28.730
Right?

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:31.360
Hey, Grandma...

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:35.420
Koume's last name is Momonose, right? 
Like pink plum blossoms, right?

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:36.460
That's right.

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:40.340
You know, they say it means "innocence."

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:44.520
Your cheeks are a childlike pink,
 like plum blossoms.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:46.900
We'll give you the name Koume.

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:50.600
They say that deep pink plum 
blossoms mean "innocence."

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:52.340
It suits you very well.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.370
Pink plum blossoms are cute, aren't they?

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:59.540
Yeah! Koume...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.090
loves her name!

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.470
My, I didn't know.

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:38.540
I had no idea Otsurusan had been a geiko.

00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:40.300
Right?

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:42.730
Oh, that anime, Pate☆Puri...

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:48.190
This says that next week the skill will 
change from "Heaven Bomber" to "Hell Bomber."

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:49.340
Hell?!

00:23:50.070 --> 00:24:10.090
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:50.070 --> 00:24:10.090
<b>"Is It Good"</b>

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:56.030
You said that when you have things to 
think about, you want to eat our sweets, right?

00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:57.370
That's weird.

00:23:57.370 --> 00:23:58.660
Don't say that.

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:02.810
Kids only get in the way.

00:24:02.810 --> 00:24:04.800
They're a handful...

00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:06.090
and they're no help with anything.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:08.570
It's crazy outside!

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:09.660
Come out and see!
